The issue is that `memory_getbuf` tries to call `PyObject_GetBuffer` on `self->view.obj`. If that's NULL or doesn't support the buffer protocol, it falls back to returning the internal view with `view->obj = NULL`. But in our case, `self->view.obj` was never set to the original object in the first place - the memoryview's internal view is already pointing to something else, which is why we're seeing that memoryview object instead of our original one.

